          "merged_at": "2026-09-18T19:02:09Z"
        },
        "body": "Full-audit regression fix.\n\nTwo previously merged scheduler protections had regressed from stable:\n- catalog work had returned to DelayQueue + synthetic 1s retry polling when catalog capacity was full;\n- ordinary failures had returned to a fixed retry delay instead of per-job adaptive backoff.\n\nThis restores the post-#225/#227 scheduler behavior while preserving current runtime features around it:\n- due catalog work waits for real released capacity instead of occupying workers / retrying every second;\n- negotiation work remains eligible while catalog capacity is full;\n- catalog slot release wakes scheduler waiters immediately;\n- catalog and negotiation failure counters stay independent;\n- adaptive retry remains 2/5/10/15m for catalog and 1/2/5/10m for negotiation, with success resetting only that job type;\n- current 120s negotiation cadence is retained;\n- current BrowserCapacityController, persisted session-block cooldowns, preview handling and browser lifecycle remain intact.\n\nRestored regression tests cover immediate capacity handoff and adaptive failure reporting/reset semantics.",
